<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Sun Intl year attrib eps flat.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Sun Intl year attrib eps flat.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre-excep	     52.9	  vs 49.8</p>
<p>    - attrib		  49.3	  vs 49.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 30.0	  vs 29.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   390.2	 vs 386.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   522.4	 vs 496.6</p>
<p>    Tax			 132.2	 vs 110.3</p>
<p>    Interest		  8.8 gain    vs 23.3 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2,336.7     vs 2,160.7</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     33.4 loss   vs nil</p>
<p>Div payable September 26</p>
<p>on register September 5</p>
<p>Full name: Sun International South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Casino to hotels group Sun International said that disposable income will remain under pressure and tourism growth will be hit by the country's crime rate.</p>
<p>Sun added that trading prospects for the coming year looked reasonably favourable due to the closure of illegal gaming operations and competitive new casinos were not seen having a significant impact on group earnings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
<p>e-mail: johannesburg.newsroom@reuters.com</p>
